	[DetailedInfoBox("Click to show warning message.", "In 2018.3, Unity introduced a new prefab workflow, and in so doing, changed how all prefabs fundamentally work. Despite our best efforts, we have so far been unable to achieve a stable implementation of Odin-serialized prefab modifications on prefab instances and variants in the new prefab workflow.This has nothing to do with Odin serializer itself, which remains rock solid. Odin-serialized ScriptableObjects and non-prefab Components/Behaviours are still perfectly stable - you are only seeing this message because this is an Odin-serialized prefab asset or instance.

We are currently in the process of doing an in-depth review of possible ways of implementing Odin-serialized modifications properly with the new prefab workflow. Meanwhile, using prefabs with Odin serialization in 2018.3 and above will be considered a *deprecated feature*.

We would like to emphasize that *our efforts may fail*. There is a real chance that we will conclude that we simply cannot support this feature any more in the new prefab workflow, in which case it will be deprecated *permanently*. We hope it won't come to that, but we sadly cannot promise that it won't happen. If we do deprecate the feature, we will not remove it, but we *will* stop supporting it. You may continue using it, but only at your own risk.

